              "For anaphylaxis, give epinephrine 1 mg/mL 0.5 mg IM in the lateral thigh; a 0.3 mg autoinjector is acceptable when that is the available device. Repeat every five minutes while significant symptoms persist.",
              "Give albuterol 2.5 mg by nebulizer for persistent bronchospasm after epinephrine; repeat every 5–15 minutes as needed to a maximum of three treatments.",
