              "For hypotension or poor perfusion, give isotonic crystalloid in 500 mL IV/IO aliquots with reassessment, maximum 2 liters. Use 250 mL aliquots when CHF, renal failure, liver failure, pulmonary edema, or volume overload is present or suspected.",
              "Continue IM epinephrine every five minutes for ongoing anaphylaxis and notify the paramedic immediately when shock, airway swelling, or refractory symptoms persist."
